1.1.text:
Article 5

Every woman has the right:

a. to obtain protection from acts of discrimination; b. to obtain protection from economic exploitation and sexual exploitation;
c. to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;
d. to obtain decent work in accordance with her abilities; e. to obtain work leave with wages/salary in accordance with statutory regulations;
f. to obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education;
g. to obtain special protection in the performance of her work or profession against matters that may threaten her safety and or health in connection with women's reproductive function; and
h. ownership and management of joint assets in marriage in accordance with statutory regulations.

Article 23

(1) The Regional Government's responsibility to prevent acts of violence against women and children includes:

a. conducting socialization on the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. providing guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children; c. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration;
d. developing an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women and children;
e. developing family empowerment programs;
f. strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. providing comfortable and safe public facilities for women and children.
(2) The prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection; f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and h. peace and order.
(3) The prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

