(1) Agencies and private parties that provide public services are required to provide lactation rooms. (2) Lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (1) are proper and adequate rooms. (3) Agency Leaders who do not provide lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (1) are subject to administrative sanctions in the form of:

a. written reprimand; and/or
b. employment sanctions based on the provisions of Statutory Regulations.
(4) Private parties who do not provide lactation rooms as referred to in paragraph (2) are subject to administrative sanctions in the form of:
a. written warning;
b. limitation of business activities;
c. freezing of business activities;
d. administrative fine; and/or e. revocation of permit.

