b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to Sub-district Heads and Nagari Guardians;

c. preparing work programs every year; d. encouraging the realization of gender-responsive planning and budgeting;

e. preparing the work plan of the Gender Mainstreaming working group every year;

f. being responsible to the Regent through the Deputy Regent; g. formulating Gender Mainstreaming policy recommendations to the Regent;

h. preparing the Regional Gender profile;

i. monitoring the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in each Regional Apparatus.

j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of gender-responsive regional budgets;

k. preparing a regional action plan on Gender Mainstreaming in the region; and

l. encouraging the selection and appointment of focal points in each Regional Apparatus.

Article 5

Every woman has the right:

a. to obtain protection from acts of discrimination; b. to obtain protection from economic exploitation and sexual exploitation;
c. to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;
d. to obtain decent work in accordance with her abilities; e. to obtain work leave with wages/salary in accordance with statutory regulations;
f. to obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education;
g. to obtain special protection in the performance of her work or profession against matters that may threaten her safety and or health in connection with women's reproductive function; and
h. ownership and management of joint assets in marriage in accordance with statutory regulations.

