a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the fulfillment of the rights of Children;
b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every Child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status of the Child, birth order of the Child, and physical and/or mental condition;
c. strengthening and developing institutions providing services for improving family quality in realizing the rights of Children;
d. guaranteeing the Protection, care, and welfare of Children by taking into account the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons who are legally responsible for the Child;
e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of the fulfillment of the rights of Children;
