l. encouraging the selection and appointment of focal points in each Regional Apparatus.

Article 18

(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point at each Regional Apparatus as referred to in Article 16 letter l consists of officials and/or staff in charge of planning and/or programs

(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the duties of:

a. promoting Gender Mainstreaming in work units;
b. facilitating the preparation of gender-responsive work plans and budgets of Regional Apparatus; c. conducting training, socialization, and advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the Regional Apparatus;
d. reporting the implementation of Gender Mainstreaming to the head of the Regional Apparatus;
e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in work units; andf. facilitating the preparation of gender data in each Regional Apparatus.
