e. encouraging the implementation of gender analysis on policies, programs, and activities in work units; andf. facilitating the preparation of gender data in each Regional Apparatus.
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and appointed by the head of the Regional Apparatus

Article 17

(1) The technical team as referred to in Article 16 letter j consists of apparatus who understand gender-responsive budget analysis.

(2) The Regional Gender Mainstreaming regional action plan as referred to in Article 16 letter k contains: a. gender mainstreaming in regional legislation;

b. gender mainstreaming in the regional development cycle;

