Article 59

(1) The Regional Government is obligated to provide comprehensive health services for Children, so that every Child obtains an optimal level of health from the womb.

(2) Comprehensive health services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative efforts for basic health services;
b. exemption from cost burden for malnourished children, children with disabilities, children with special needs, children infected with HIV/ AIDS, child laborers, child victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic and other addictive substance abuse, children who are victims of violence, and child victims of trafficking in persons;
(3) The Regional Government, community, families and parents must endeavor to ensure that Children who are born avoid diseases that threaten survival and/or cause disability.

