Article 60

(1) Promotive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 59 paragraph (2) letter a are aimed at improving the level of health more optimally.

(2) Promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by providing socialization or education to the community regarding healthy lifestyles which include:

a. the importance of exclusive breastfeeding for babies;
b. the importance of immunization for toddlers;
c. clean living patterns;
d. the importance of nutritious food; and e. the dangers of drugs and smoking.
(3) In addition to promotive efforts as referred to in paragraph (2), the Regional Government may conduct other activities in the context of health provision.

Article 12

(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:

a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. implementing Gender Mainstreaming in the Region; c. establishing a Gender Mainstreaming working group in the Region; d. enhancing Women's Empowerment in role, quality and capacity in the fields of:
1. politics;
2. law;
3. social; and
4. economy.
e. strengthening and developing women's empowerment service provider institutions in the region. (2) The responsibility of the regional government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the relevant Regional Apparatus.

